      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It looks like this in the log:\n2020.09.18 07:39:52 Exception  -  NullReferenceException: Object reference not set to an instance of an object.\nVRCNetworkBehaviour.ǅǄǅǄǅǅǄǄǄǅǅǅǄǅǄǄǅǅǅǅǄǄǄǅǅǅǅǅǅǅǅǄǄǄǅǅǄǅǄǅǄǅǄǅǅǄǄ () (at <00000000000000000000000000000000>:0)\nVRC.Networking.UdonSync+ǄǄǄǄǄǅǅǅǄǄǄǄǄǅǅǄǄǄǅǄǅǄǄǅǅǄǄǄǄǅǄǅǅǅǅǅǅǄǄǄǄǅǄǄǄǅǄ.MoveNext () (at <00000000000000000000000000000000>:0)\nUnityEngine.SetupCoroutine.InvokeMoveNext (System.Collections.IEnumerator enumerator, System.IntPtr returnValueAddress) (at <00000000000000000000000000000000>:0)\nBut lag seems to have nothing to do with this. The way to eliminate this error is to delay the destruction of the object for a period of time (even if the object does not run any synchronization components)\n@{5de9405aea7cc52772fcc359|full_name}",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
